@startuml UC-P1-create-a-project-analysis-sequence
!include ../../domain/diagrams/_style.puml
hide footbox
title UC-P1 Create a project (analysis: system sequence)
' Analysis level (decision 9): the person and Playground as one box. No outside system takes part.
' It is split from the design because a security rule shapes the steps (an administrator is not a member of
' the project they create, RULE-P2). No route, store, port, adapter, token or cookie.
' Step numbers are the main flow numbers of UC-P1.
' Not drawn: the order of the refusals, and whether a refused creation is audited (open questions 3 and 4),
' and a manager who names a manager (open question 1).

actor "Administrator\nor manager" as U
participant "Playground" as PG #E6F0FB

U -> PG : 1 create a project\n(name, manager)
alt not an administrator,\nmanages no project
  PG --> U : 2 refused
else
  alt name empty or over 100
    PG --> U : 3 refused
  else an administrator who manages no project
    alt no manager, not active,\nor the administrator
      PG --> U : 4 refused
    else
      PG -> PG : 5 create it,\nnamed person is manager,\nadministrator is no member
    end
  else a person who manages a project
    PG -> PG : 5 create it,\nthe person is manager
  end
end
PG -> PG : 6 record who and\nwho the manager is
PG --> U : 7 the new project
@enduml
